^[a-z]{1,}[a-z0-9:]{1,}/[a-z0-9]{0,}\\[a-z]{1,}$

conditions:-
1. starts with any character between a-z only.
2.then any number, any alphabet and ':' characters only of any length.
3.then '/' character
4. then zero or more characters of either alphabet or digit type only.
5.then '\' character
6. then any character between a-z of any length.

Ex:-
xyz123c:bv/12abvc12\abc


Also we do have below syntax in RegEx.
[^a-z] :- any character except a-z
\w:- matches alphanumeric and underscore character
\W:- matches characters that are neither alphanumeric nor underscore 
\s:- matches whitespace character (tab, space) 
\S:- matches non whitespace character
\d:- matches digit 
\D- non digit match 
*:- matches 0 or more of the preceding token
 
Now suppose we have to validate password. Criteria of password as follows.
Minimum length 8 characters.
Must start with alphabet
Must contain at least an upper case and a lower case character and a number
Must contain a special character out of *,#,_
Our regular expression will look like as below.
Ex:-
regexPattern = @"^(?=\S*[a-z])(?=\S*[A-Z])(?=\S*\d)(?=\S*[^\w\s])\S{8,}$";
 
 Here (?=) represent positive look ahead. Meaning input must contain character(s) defined after "?=".
(?=\S*[a-z]) :- must contain a-z without whitespace
(?=\S*[A-Z]):- must contain A-Z without whitespace
(?=\S*\d):- must contain any number without whitespace
(?=\S*[^\w\s]):- must contain any character except word (alphanumeric and underscore) and whitespace
\S{8,}:- minimum character length as 8 without whitespace
